        "question": {
          ":question/id": "caf86b76-43dd-52e9-bc58-faa3a2bfa0df",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
          ":question/problem": "Calculate the length of the altitude $RH$ of $\\triangle PQR$, where $P(-1,-2,2)$, $Q(-1,-2,4)$, $R(2,-1,1)$. Here $H$ is the foot of the perpendicular from $R$ to the line $PQ$.",
          ":question/worked-solution": "The altitude $RH$ corresponds to the base $PQ$, so\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A_{\\triangle PQR}=\\frac12 PQ\\cdot RH.\n$$\n\nForm the required edge vectors from the vertices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{PQ}&=\\langle -1-(-1),-2-(-2),4-2\\rangle,\\\\\n&=\\langle 0,0,2\\rangle.\\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PR}&=\\langle 2-(-1),-1-(-2),1-2\\rangle,\\\\\n&=\\langle 3,1,-1\\rangle.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate the cross product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{PQ}\\times \\overrightarrow{PR}&=\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf i&\\mathbf j&\\mathbf k\\\\0&0&2\\\\3&1&-1\\end{vmatrix}\\\\\nw_1&=0\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 1=-2,\\\\\nw_2&=2\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-1)=6,\\\\\nw_3&=0\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3=0,\\\\\n\\overrightarrow{PQ}\\times \\overrightarrow{PR}&=\\langle -2,6,0\\rangle.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe magnitude of the cross product gives the parallelogram area:\n\n$$\n\\left|\\overrightarrow{PQ}\\times \\overrightarrow{PR}\\right|=\\sqrt{(-2)^2+6^2+0^2}=2 \\sqrt{10}.\n$$\n\nThe matching base length is\n\n$$\nPQ=\\sqrt{0^2+0^2+2^2}=2.\n$$\n\nThe triangle has half the parallelogram area:\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A_{\\triangle PQR}=\\frac12\\left(2 \\sqrt{10}\\right)=\\sqrt{10}.\n$$\n\nSubstitute the area and matching base, then solve for the altitude:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{10}&=\\frac12\\left(2\\right)RH,\\\\\n2 \\sqrt{10}&=\\left(2\\right)RH,\\\\\nRH&=\\frac{2 \\sqrt{10}}{2}=\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe altitude is $\\sqrt{10}$ units.",
